# Install to /etc/portage/package.use/cmus
#
# Every flag here is in media-sound/cmus-2.12.0's IUSE. `wma` and
# `zsh-completion` are NOT cmus flags (WMA goes through ffmpeg; the zsh
# completion ships as a contrib script), so they must not be listed here or
# Portage warns on every emerge.
#
# pulseaudio is added deliberately: cmus needs an output that reaches
# wireplumber, otherwise it only has ALSA/OSS.
# elogind is what gives cmus its MPRIS interface, which is how the bar's
# now-playing chip sees it without the cmus-remote fallback.
media-sound/cmus aac cddb cdio discid elogind ffmpeg mp4 musepack pidgin pulseaudio
